Author: Wallace Chan <naahtec@hotmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jun 11 18:03:52 2026 -0400

    skill: #11329 AC1+AC4 — event_poll nudge-only + model-B test migration
    
    Migrate event_poll.py to the canonical model-B (AGENT-RUNTIME §8.0/§8.1):
    event_poll emits a bare NUDGE\n and never touches the cursor. The agent
    owns per-event ack-cursor; the harness owns .event-state.json. event_poll
    tracks only a private in-memory high-water-mark to edge-trigger one nudge
    per new batch.
    
    AC1 — drop the per-event JSON-emit + working-state cursor write; remove
    _read_cursor_from_working_state / _write_cursor_atomic / _resolve_cursor /
    _working_state_path / _CURSOR_LINE_PREFIX; emit a single NUDGE on
    non-empty/evicted; poll() returns (events, next_since). Eviction now nudges
    the agent to recover (no event_poll re-anchor) and advances the local hwm
    past the gap.
    
    AC4 — reframe the suites for model B: assert NUDGE-not-JSON, cursor
    independence, hwm advancement, eviction-nudge. Delete the obsolete #9740
    eviction-cursor-race file (event_poll no longer writes the cursor, so the
    race is structurally impossible). e2e long-lag/eviction invariants now
    exercise the harness GET (the agent's path) directly. Reworded eviction
    diagnostic: "advancing to" -> "nudging agent to recover past".
    
    Resolves the doc-vs-runtime contradiction operator-ratified 2026-06-11:
    #11329's AC text (event_poll acks) was stale vs the post-#11328-D2 model
    (agent acks). See #11329 comment.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>

